Cleanup: the demo http.server (port 8471) was killed; pgrep confirms no
  match and the port is closed. Correction logged, not smoothed: the first
  kill used `pkill -f "http.server 8471"`, whose pattern matched the killing
  shell's own command line and SIGTERM'd the exec session itself; the server
  was verified gone afterward with a non-self-matching pgrep pattern.

--- RE-RUN 2026-10-10: nmap, Semgrep, Playwright now installed on this machine ---
Install notes (2026-10-10, Ubuntu noble container, root):
- apt-get update hangs on this machine's mirrors (fetches stall; zero-CPU hang),
  so packages were fetched as .debs via curl from archive.ubuntu.com and
  installed with dpkg. nmap needed: nmap-common, liblinear4, liblua5.4-0,
  libpcap0.8t64, libssh2-1t64, libibverbs1, libnl-route-3-200, libnl-3-200.
- Playwright: pip install playwright (PEP 668: --break-system-packages);
  `playwright install chromium` reused the cached chromium-1243 build.
- Semgrep: system pip refused (typing_extensions RECORD conflict with the
  Debian-shipped copy); installed cleanly in a venv
  (.gap-sprint/semvenv). The earlier "dead shim" report is superseded —
  the engine runs.

